// ADR 0066 M1.1: `Task<T>` generalised beyond the ADR 0024 `Task<i64>`-only
// restriction. This spawns a worker that takes an `i32` argument and returns
// an `f64` result — exercising the two trickiest cases at once:
//
//   * the per-spawn wrapper loads the arg with its REAL type (`i32`), not the
//     old hard-coded `i64`;
//   * the wrapper ENCODES the `f64` result into the Task's `i64` result slot
//     (a `bitcast`), and `.await` DECODES it back to `f64` (the inverse).
//
// The runtime `SentinelTask.result` slot stays `i64`, so there is no ABI
// change and existing `Task<i64>` IR is byte-identical (the i64 case encodes
// to a no-op).
//
// Trace: `spawn dbl(21)` runs `(21 as f64) * 2.0 = 42.0` on a worker thread;
// `.await` decodes 42.0; `r as i64` truncates to 42. The scope discharges the
// Async effect so `main` stays effect-free. Exit 42.
//
// snc-only demonstrator (f64 is snc-side per ADR 0058) — OUT of the scg
// differential; the selfhost mirror + a `tests/pass/c66` differential fixture
// (over a selfhost-supported type) land in M1.1 Phase B.
//
// Expected: exit code 42, no stdout.

fn dbl(x: i32) -> f64 ! { Async } {
    (x as f64) * 2.0
}

fn main() -> i64 {
    let r: f64 = scope concurrent {
        let t = spawn dbl(21 as i32);
        t.await
    };
    r as i64
}
